Content-Type: text/plain;
  charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
Content-Disposition: inline

Now that we have two architectures that are no longer official release=20
architectures I've been wondering if we should remove any architecture-=20
specific text for them from the Installation Guide.

m68k was dropped as a release architecture for Etch, and alpha is being=20
dropped for Squeeze. For m68k the intention was to bring it back as a=20
release architecture, but now, over 2 years later, I think we can say=20
that's unlikely to happen.

The current situation is that both alpha and m68k are still included in the=
=20
source for the manual, but are not included in official builds and also=20
not in the "daily" builds on Alioth. So effectively it is dead text.

I know that the installer still supports m68k (and is even being maintained=
=20
to some extend by Steven Marenka) and that the same may or may not happen=20
for alpha, but IMO that's a separate issue.
A fact is that there have been no updates for the manual for either=20
architecture for a very long time and that for example any links to images=
=20
in them are incorrect.

The main benefit of removing the architectures is for translators,=20
especially for new translations. It would remove 2000+ lines of text which=
=20
would no longer need to be translated (and which probably nobody will ever=
=20
read anyway).

If we do decide on the removal I would try to do it as four separate=20
commits for each architecture:
=2D remove the arch from the English original
=2D remove the arch from all XML based translations [1]
=2D remove the arch from the build system
=2D PO files update, including removal of arch conditions embedded in strin=
gs
  (if any)

Doing it this way would still keep open the option of re-including an arch=
=20
later by reverting the first three of those commits.
Of course, there would be some conflicts that would need to be handled and=
=20
a general review and update would be needed, but I expect most text could=20
be recovered without too many problems.
=46or PO-based translations a PO-file merge could be done of the then curre=
nt=20
version with the version just before removal.

Opinions, comments and suggestions welcome.

Cheers,
=46JP

[1] I expect I can do all changes myself, both for the English original and=
=20
for translations; mostly using a script plus minor manual work for=20
remaining bits. So there should be no work needed by translators.

--nextPart1773758.oS823dza2L
